{fmt} 11.2.0 (https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt), formatting library. MIT license, see LICENSE.

Needed only by mp-units (external/mp-units), and only with standard libraries without <format>, such as libstdc++
of gcc 12 (Debian 12, e.g. at GSI): mp-units then uses {fmt} instead of std::format. THERMINATOR itself does not
use it. With gcc 13 or newer it is not used.

Only the headers are included here, unchanged:
  include/fmt  <- include/fmt of the release
Source: https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt/archive/refs/tags/11.2.0.tar.gz
        sha256 bc23066d87ab3168f27cef3e97d545fa63314f5c79df5ea444d41d56f962c6af

Used header-only, without CMake and without building the library: the Makefile adds include/ and -DFMT_HEADER_ONLY.
